{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send screen-opened and state-transition events to any analytics backend with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every screen that models its state with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"text":" already knows exactly when it was opened and when it moves between Empty, Loading, Data, and Error. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService"},{"text":" turns those moments into ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent"},{"text":"s and fans them out to as many ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker"},{"text":"s as you register — one per analytics backend (Firebase, Mixpanel, Amplitude, your own logging endpoint, a debug console print, …).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"ScreenStates ships no backend-specific tracker implementations, so the core module stays dependency-free — but it does include ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (logs every event to the console) and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (silently discards everything), so you don’t have to hand-roll a console logger just to confirm events fire at the right moments. For a real backend, write one small adapter, converting the event’s backend-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/AnalyticsValue","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" parameters into that SDK’s own format:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct FirebaseScreenTracker: ScreenAnalyticsTracker {","    func track(_ event: ScreenAnalyticsEvent) {","        Analytics.logEvent(event.name, parameters: event.parameters.mapValues { value in","            switch value {","            case .string(let string): string","            case .int(let int): int","            case .double(let double): double","            case .bool(let bool): bool","            }","        })","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An adapter is also free to remap ","type":"text"},{"code":"event.name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to whatever vocabulary its backend expects — Firebase, for example, reserves a specific constant for screen views.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Wiring-a-screen","type":"heading","text":"Wiring a screen"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let analytics = ScreenAnalyticsService(trackers: [FirebaseScreenTracker(), PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker()])","","func onAppear(source: ScreenOpenSource<AppScreen>) {","    analytics.trackScreenOpened(\"Articles\", source: source.analyticsKind)","    analytics.observeStateChanges(of: store, screen: \"Articles\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreenOpened(_:source:)"},{"type":"text","text":" sends one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_opened"},{"type":"text","text":" event. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withObservationTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" mechanism "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" uses to mirror a store, and sends a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_state_changed"},{"type":"text","text":" event for every subsequent "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" transition — call it once, right where you create or first observe the store. When a transition lands on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", the event also carries the error’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It also times how long the screen spends in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":": the moment the state leaves "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", it sends a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_load_duration"},{"type":"text","text":" event ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenLoadDuration(screen:outcome:milliseconds:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") with that outcome and the elapsed time in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration_ms"},{"text":" — useful for a “how long do loads actually take, and how often do they end in an error” dashboard without hand-rolling a stopwatch around every ","type":"text"},{"code":"load(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"screen_state_changed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" event landing on ","type":"text"},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tells you a screen failed to load; it doesn’t tell you whether the user gave up or hit Retry. Call ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenRetryTapped(screen:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") from the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure you pass to the Error placeholder, so that’s a distinct, countable event instead of indistinguishable from the screen’s initial ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateView(store.state, onRetry: {","    analytics.trackRetryTapped(\"Articles\")","    Task { await store.load { try await api.fetchArticles() } }","}) { articles in","    ArticleList(articles)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadNextPage(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t move "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" off "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" on either a success or a failure, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)"},{"type":"text","text":" has nothing to report for it — call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackNextPageLoaded(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackNextPageFailed(_:errorDescription:)"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageLoaded(screen:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageFailed(screen:errorDescription:)"},{"type":"text","text":") from the same place you call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadNextPage(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", mirroring how "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is called from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func loadMore() async {","    await store.loadNextPage { try await api.fetchArticles(page: nextPage) }","    if let error = store.loadNextPageError {","        analytics.trackNextPageFailed(\"Articles\", errorDescription: error.localizedDescription)","    } else {","        analytics.trackNextPageLoaded(\"Articles\")","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" expose an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"analyticsKind"},{"type":"text","text":" helper — a short, stable, payload-free name for the current case ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"loading\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"error\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"push\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"deep_link\""},{"type":"text","text":", …) — so you can build custom "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"s yourself for anything the built-in factories don’t cover."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/d